# RFC #362 desktop.16 · E1 round review and undo (agent-rounds).
#
# An Agent turn's canvas writes are recorded in a per-turn ledger
# (agent-runs/<turn>.changes.jsonl, one line per applied undoable command, with
# its project event cursor and the objects it changed). The ledger is written in
# AgentTools.execute right after the command commits; a ledger failure is logged
# and never fails the committed write.
#
#  * application/agent_rounds.py: round_changes() joins the ledger with the
#    authoritative history states; undo_round() replays history.undo for the
#    still-applied writes newest first, passing the current revisions of the
#    touched objects as expectedVersions. The field-level history check still
#    rejects any edit made later by the user; the first rejection stops the round
#    and is reported, nothing is overwritten silently.
#  * api: GET /assistant/turns/{turn}/changes (read-only) and
#    POST /assistant/turns/{turn}/undo (window lease required; refused with 409
#    while an Agent run is active for the project).
#  * web: a review line under a finished Agent reply ("N changes this round",
#    two-step "Undo this round"), zh-CN and en-US.
#  * fixture: creation_server.py routes canvas:<title> writes through the real
#    ToolGateway so the browser journey exercises the production ledger path.
#
# Verification: tests/test_agent_rounds.py (4 cases: newest-first undo, a later user
# edit is never overwritten, empty round, non-undoable writes not recorded);
# agent/creation pytest subset 755 passed; verification/agent_round_undo.mjs PASS
# zh-CN and en-US (2 writes recorded, 2 undone); npm run check:i18n and build pass.
